## Nexus Core — server configuration
##
## Generated by the txAdmin deployment recipe.
##
## Values marked OPERATOR MUST SUPPLY are blank on purpose. Fill them in on your
## server. Never commit a filled-in copy to a repository: a credential in a
## repository is published, and rotation is the only remedy.

{{serverEndpoints}}

sv_hostname "{{serverName}}"
sets sv_projectName "{{serverName}}"
sets sv_projectDesc "{{recipeDescription}}"
sets locale "en-US"
sets tags "roleplay, nexus core, custom framework"

sv_maxclients {{maxClients}}
sv_licenseKey "{{svLicense}}"
sv_scriptHostBind "0.0.0.0"
sv_enforceGameBuild 3095

set steam_webApiKey "none"

## ------------------------------------------------------------------ database
## OPERATOR MUST SUPPLY. Format:
##   mysql://<USER>:<PASSWORD>@<HOST>/<DATABASE>?charset=utf8mb4
## The angle brackets are placeholders. Replace the whole value.
set mysql_connection_string ""

## --------------------------------------------------------------- Nexus Core
## Bootstrap configuration only. Everything operational — business hours,
## payouts, prices, target locations, dispatch rules — is registered by each
## resource and edited in game through a permission-controlled interface.

## Environment identity: development, staging, or production.
set nxc_environment "development"

## Core startup mode: normal or recovery.
set nxc_startup_mode "normal"

## OPERATOR MUST SUPPLY. Signing key for session and NUI tokens.
## Generate a unique value per environment. Rotating it invalidates live sessions.
set nxc_token_signing_key ""

## Log level: debug, info, warn, error. debug is disabled in production.
set nxc_log_level "info"

## Development diagnostics. MUST be false in production: nxc_devtools exposes
## internal state, and a diagnostics tool reachable in production is an
## information-disclosure vulnerability.
set nxc_dev_mode "false"

## ------------------------------------------------------------------- startup
## Resources start in dependency order. A resource must not assume a later
## resource is available.

ensure oxmysql
ensure pma-voice
ensure screenshot-basic

## Nexus Core foundation. The full order is:
##   nxc_lib -> nexus_core -> nxc_config -> nxc_ui -> nxc_zones -> nxc_target
##   -> nxc_interact -> nxc_devtools
## Only published resources are listed. The rest are added as each is released.

ensure nxc_lib
